phi-adapter-sdk (0.15.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Actions say where and how they are offered in typed fields:
    placement (Card, Field, Device, Hidden), kind, requiresAck,
    loadFormOnOpen, submitLabel, resultField, timeoutMs and a confirm
    struct. metaJson and confirmJson on the descriptor are gone.
  * A form field's number bounds, appendTo and reloadsForm are members;
    the field has no metaJson any more. AdapterCapabilities::defaultsJson
    is gone: defaults are the fields' defaultValue.
  * Structured results are typed: ActionResultType::Display (text, code,
    qr), Run (a streamed run) and Data (dataJson, for tools). resultValueJson
    is gone.
  * sendAdapterMetaUpdated takes AdapterFormValues; a null removes the
    key. What only the adapter reads back goes to stateDirectory() with
    readStateFile / writeStateFile.
  * formValuesFromJson turns action params into form values.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Tue, 15 Sep 2026 14:46:50 +0200

phi-adapter-sdk (0.14.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * A form says what it means, not how many grid units it takes. The
    schema drops span/labelSpan/controlSpan/actionSpan, gridUnits, gutter
    and the section defaults; a dialog now chooses width, columns (1-3)
    and labelWidth from one size scale (Narrow/Normal/Wide), a field its
    cells, newRow, controlWidth, and Auto/Top/None label and Auto/Below
    button positions. The client owns the numbers.
  * Buttons belong to a field as an `actions` list; field type Action
    becomes Actions (a row of buttons), Section is a type of its own.
  * choicesFrom and perChoiceOf replace the meta keys choiceSubsetOf and
    valueChangeUpdates.
  * The SDK writes the schema, form value and choice JSON:
    AdapterFactory::configSchema() returns an AdapterConfigSchema, and
    ActionResponse carries typed formValues and fieldChoices. The
    hand-written configSchemaJson/formValuesJson/fieldChoicesJson are gone.
  * Actions with a form carry formLayout in the descriptor.

