phi-adapter-sdk (0.13.3-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * An instance is configured before its start() runs. The
    config.changed that creates the instance was handed over only after
    start() returned, so a setting read in start() always took its
    default. The Matter adapter reads the HCI index there, because the
    CHIP stack wants it before the controller comes up, and BLE
    commissioning therefore stayed off however the instance was
    configured.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:57:04 +0200

phi-adapter-sdk (0.13.2-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * HttpClient clears OpenSSL's thread-local error queue before each TLS
    call and does not shut down a session whose handshake never finished.
    Two clients on one thread (a poll and an event stream) otherwise read
    each other's leftovers as failures: "shutdown while in init" ended a
    healthy stream at hue's start.

